# Inkling 2 Mini (stock), Basalt NVFP4-MX8: the RTX 5090 default since
# 2026-11-24 (Max; docs/reports/DECISIONS-2026-11-24.md §10).
#
# The serve args and agent setup of the measured row INK-T2-STOCK (campaign
# arm I_T2_stock, 53/71 scored, SCORE 78.2, single seed): Basalt v0.5.7
# (400b411c), the stock pack jesdga/Inkling-2-Mini-Basalt @
# c2afac3adb772e14d77b2ea2ac7068ad4460e932, file
# Inkling-2-Mini-NVFP4-MX8.basalt, sha256 28ec7072…1b99, 19,606,374,189
# bytes (evals/boards/v5/weights.json inkling2-mini-basalt-nvfp4-mx8-stock;
# pinned in scripts/weights.registry), served as
#   basalt serve --alias inkling-2-mini --parallel 1 --max-context 262144 --kv fp8
# with DSpark at the pack's default draft length (no flag) and the answer room
# at Basalt's default (auto: min(max(512, cap//4), cap//2) output tokens kept
# for the answer, so 6,144 thinking tokens of an 8,192-token turn). Those are
# the args `docker inspect` read at the arm's start and end
# (weights.json evidence). The serve record: the V5 Inkling report §10.1.
#
# NOT exactly that row: the BUILD. INK-T2-STOCK ran the unpatched pin; this
# profile serves the pin plus the PR #632 patch (PATCHES below), per
# DECISIONS-2026-11-24 §11 ("whenever we serve Inkling 2 Mini on Basalt").
# No board row has measured pin + #632 with these args, and the Strata
# report §16.6 probe saw the patch at --answer-room auto end more replies at
# the 8,192 cap while still writing their call (9 of 12, unpatched 5): the
# reason arm I_T3 pairs the patch with --answer-room 8192 (and a 16,384 cap).
# I_T3 (INK-T3, 52/71) did not settle the answer room: it bundled the patch,
# 8,192 answer room, a 16,384 cap and wall-bound turns, scored level with
# INK-T2-STOCK, and lost 4 units to context overflow (DECISIONS-2026-11-25
# §4; V5_INKLING2_MINI_I_T3-2026-11-25). So ANSWER_ROOM stays auto; the open
# item is an arm of this exact build (docs/TODO.md "Basalt after the switch").
# Change it, PATCHES and MEASURED_ROW here, with the arm that measured them,
# never in the adapter. The launch refuses a build whose
# patches differ from PATCHES.
#
# Parsed by scripts/engines/basalt.sh (KEY=VALUE, never sourced).
PACK=Inkling-2-Mini-NVFP4-MX8.basalt
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=inkling-2-mini
PARALLEL=1
MAX_CONTEXT=262144
KV=fp8
ANSWER_ROOM=auto
# The agent setup measured with it (scripts/lib/conf.sh _ob_profile_set).
AGENT_PROFILE=inkling-best
# The board row whose serve args and agent setup these are
# (evals/boards/v5/board.json); its build was the unpatched pin (above).
MEASURED_ROW=INK-T2-STOCK
# The local patches the serving build must carry, exactly ('none' = the pin).
PATCHES=basalt-pr632-55f9be17.patch
